m. The CRP contract continues through September 30, 2036, at an annual payment rate of $42.24 per acre, producing approximately $13,255 in annual contract income. The buyer will receive the landlord’s 88% share of the 2027 and future CRP payments. This tract offers the benefits of established annual income, reduced management requirements, conservation value and potential recreational or wildlife habitat appeal, subject to the existing CRP contract and USDA regulations.,,All of the seller’s mineral interests, including the existing oil production on Tract 1, will transfer to the respective buyers. The seller will retain the landlord’s share of the 2026 milo crop. Buyers will receive the landlord’s one-third share of the 2027 wheat crop planted this fall. Future FSA payments will follow the crops and be paid pursuant to applicable FSA regulations. Possession will be granted following harvest on acreage planted to milo, at closing on the CRP acreage and following the 2027 wheat harvest on acreage planted to wheat this fall.,,The successful bidders will pay 10% down on the day of the auction, with the balance due at closing on or before November 19, 2026, or upon completion of title requirements. Bidding is not contingent upon financing. Bidders may participate in person, online or by telephone; all internet and telephone bidders must register and receive approval before the auction. This absolute auction represents a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial block of Lane County, Kansas land with productive cropland, long-term CRP income and transferable oil royalty interests. Contact Donald L. Hazlett, Broker/Auctioneer, at 785-443-1299 or Farm & Ranch Realty, Inc. at 1-800-247-7863 for complete auction terms, tract information, mineral production records and bidding assistance.",
